# libmmt's canonical negative catalog corpus, as `<git blob SHA>  <file name>`.
#
# `negative/` is declared a byte-identical mirror of libmmt's
# packages/container/test-vectors/catalog/negative/, and `negative-local/` holds
# only negatives libmmt does NOT ship. Both were prose contracts until this file
# existed: nothing compared the directories against libmmt's actual listing, and
# the mirror was broken twice — once by a hand edit, once by a merge that
# carried three local-only fixtures into `negative/` with every local signal
# (directory/registry consistency, arity, rejection behaviour) still green.
#
# A git blob SHA is a content hash, so equality here is byte-identity. Vendoring
# the listing keeps the check a pure local comparison — no network at test time,
# and no dependency on libmmt being checked out beside this repo.
#
# This file is the thing you update when you deliberately sync. Regenerate it
# from a libmmt checkout (it prints exactly the payload lines below):
#
#   git ls-tree origin/main -- packages/container/test-vectors/catalog/negative/ \
#     | awk '{ n = $4; sub(/.*\//, "", n); print $3 "  " n }' | sort -k2
#
